  "footnote": "Source: company 10-Q and 10-K filings (Apr 2024 to Jul 2026), research team analysis. Four-firm total, cash basis",
  "notes": "Taken together, the four's capex rose from 45% of operating cash flow in Q1 2024 to 96% in Q2 2026. The difference between the two, roughly what is left after the build-out, fell from $54.7bn to $6.7bn. In Q2 the four generated about $171.8bn of operating cash and spent about $165bn in cash capex. Full-year guidance means the second half adds tens of billions more a quarter, so operating cash would have to jump to keep up. That is why the next pages show debt, equity and long leases. Company by company the ratio is higher still: Alphabet was at 115% in Q2 and Amazon at 138% in the first half, both above their own operating cash flow."
